                    Transcribed by Bernau.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d125-f2" n="2" xml:id="d125-f2-content">
                <p>Reference is to Ben Gurion’s message to
                        Eisenhower in telegram 990, <ref
                        target="#d124"><hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi></ref></p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d125-f3" n="3" xml:id="d125-f3-content">
                <p>At 2:58 p.m. on February 21, Dulles sent
                        Lawson the following Niact cable: “Regret probably impossible further
                    postpone UN consideration but will strive delay
                    formulation there of US position and final UN
                    action until Eban returns.” (Telegram 812
                    to Tel Aviv, February 21; Department of State, Central Files,
                    674.84A/2–2157)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
